module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.absorbing_fallback

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data absorbing_fallback: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "absorbing_fallback" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "LATENT COMPATIBILITY INSTANCE: gunbc.host_memory_qualification implication_severity mapped EvidenceUnobserved to PartNotImplicated, and product.build_fulfillment compatibility_of promoted that negative screen to CompatibilityEstablished. The composition could establish compatibility without evidence, but compatibility_of had no production callers and no purchasing actuator reached it. This is a declared-but-uncalled seam, repaired before the prospective evaluator consumes it. PartEvidenceUnresolved now carries the missing step, while compatibility_of consumes both unresolved evidence and a non-implication as CompatibilityEvidenceUnread, leaving policy to resolve_supplied_line. HostMemoryStanding keeps class support, part qualification, training and boot independent. Executing discriminator: test.claim.host_memory_qualification_witness_test unobserved_evidence_never_establishes_purchasing_compatibility; direct fulfillment-policy witness: test.claim.build_fulfillment_witness w_unread_compatibility_is_pending_evidence_not_a_purchase. The widening arm admitted silent wrongness under direct invocation; the executed claims establish mechanical prevention only for source-to-interpretation of these functions, not for a production purchasing decision or an emitted target. Positive compatibility for an actual part and population remains an external evidence obligation, not something a negative failure screen can prove.",
    "absorbing fallback (a failure arm that widens — rerun everything, scan all keys, always run — instead of refusing; ⊤-as-answer conflated with ⊤-as-ignorance; the deficit's frequency zeroed by construction, the corpus-denominated cost breaking the budget later)",
    "UPSTREAM INSTANCE, 2026-09-07, and it governed this fleet's serving behaviour for weeks. vLLM's `EngineArgs.get_batch_defaults` probes the device for its memory and wraps the probe in a bare `except Exception: device_memory = 0`, commented 'This is only used to set default_max_num_batched_tokens'. On a GB10 the memory is UNIFIED, `nvmlDeviceGetMemoryInfo` returns NVML_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED, and the handler writes zero — so the `device_memory >= 70 * GiB` test fails and a 121.7 GiB machine takes the small-device branch, selecting max_num_batched_tokens 2048 for the OpenAI-server context. The CUDA runtime reports the pool correctly (130,663,231,488 bytes); only the NVML path refuses.",
    "WHAT MAKES IT THIS CLASS RATHER THAN AN ORDINARY BUG: nothing failed, nothing was counted, and the substituted value is PLAUSIBLE. 2048 is a real default that a real small device would legitimately receive, so the resulting configuration is indistinguishable by inspection from a deliberate one — which is why three separate analyses reasoned about the budget without anyone suspecting how it had been chosen. The comment is the author explaining why the absorption was judged harmless, and the judgement was made about the ASSIGNMENT rather than about the decision the value goes on to govern.",
    "THE MEASURED COST, so the class carries a price and not only a mechanism: a 1,048,576-token-context model served on a 2048-token prefill budget. Because chunked prefill runs as a mixed batch, a co-tenant decoder receives one token per chunk, so its inter-token latency IS the step duration — measured at 30.1ms alone against 2168.2ms beside a cold prefill, a ~72x degradation, which is what users experienced as ~0.4 tokens per second. The value turns out to be defensible for the interactive objective among the arms that were measured, which is luck rather than design: nobody chose it, and it moves the moment the probe, the driver or the hardware changes. Rows at extdeps.vllm.batch_defaults and gunbc.spark.prefill_batch_sweep.",
    "THE SCOPE OF THIS INSTANCE IS PLATFORM TIMES RUNTIME REVISION, NOT THE HARDWARE ALONE, and saying otherwise is how a dated reading becomes standing authority. What was established is that THIS vLLM revision, on a GB10, resolves the batch default through a device-memory probe it catches and zeroes. The path does not consult the model, so it should reproduce for any checkpoint served by the same build -- and a DIFFERENT IMAGE MUST REACQUIRE IT rather than inherit it, which is the same rule the cumulative_metric_read_as_per_event row states for metric semantics: ask the installed binary, not the upstream repository. The durable remedy is not knowing the default; it is pinning the budget explicitly so no default is consulted.",
    "**A WIDENING THAT PRODUCES A CALMING SENTENCE IS HARDER TO SEE THAN ONE THAT PRODUCES AN ALARMING NUMBER.** This row's other receipts widen into VALUES -- a zero, a superset, a plausible literal -- and a value invites the question \"where did that come from\". The same defect in PROSE does not, because the output is a sentence asserting that everything is in order, and nobody audits reassurance. Both are the same fail-open; only one of them looks like data.",

    "SPECIMEN, gunbc#11193 (found by review 66208, 2026-09-14), AND ITS VALUE IS THE PAIR RATHER THAN THE INSTANCE. The SAME AUTHOR, on the SAME BRANCH, on the SAME DAY, wrote both halves. Review 65676 caught the first: a sibling component whose footprint was unread CONTRIBUTED ZERO to a memory-budget subtraction, defended on direction -- a larger budget can only miss an exclusion, never invent one -- and the repair made it REFUSE. Hours later, one function away, `pool_relief_standing` read a `false` from a predicate over an EMPTY hop chain and asserted the sentence \"the token-time hop of X has a derived placement inside the memory pool\" about a route with no resolvable token-time hop at all, and carried it to the product root through the component's accelerator standing. A route naming a provider the roster does not admit was reported as a route whose bytes are comfortably in the pool.",

    "WHY THE FIRST REPAIR DID NOT PREVENT THE SECOND, which is the transferable part: the repair taught the shape in ONE DIRECTION. Having learned that an unread quantity must not become a zero, the author did not generalise to an unresolved STRUCTURE must not become a placement claim. The empty chain was even defended in a comment -- correctly -- as honest for the PREDICATES over it, whose true answer is \"no hops with that property\"; what the comment did not say is that a non-predicate consumer converts that silence into an affirmative. The same asymmetry as auditing what a module USES from an import rather than what the import PROVIDES.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE FOR THE PROSE FORM: for every arm that RENDERS A SENTENCE rather than returning a value, ask what input reaches it by DEFAULT rather than by establishment -- an empty list, a false predicate, an absent lookup. If the sentence it emits would be FALSE for that input and REASSURING to a reader, it is this class. The tell is an `if !p(x)` whose body asserts the positive of p rather than reporting that p could not be established; the fix is a fourth arm checked BEFORE the branch, carrying the located reason, so the unresolved case has its own spelling instead of borrowing the healthy one.",

    "**FOUR INSTANCES ON ONE BRANCH, ONE CLASS: AN UNKNOWN PROMOTED TO A DEFINITE.** gunbc#11193, 2026-09-14. Each arm below had a value or a sentence standing where the honest answer was \"not established\", and each was individually plausible enough to survive authoring, self-review and at least one approving review. Listed together because the pattern is invisible one instance at a time: (1) an unread SIBLING FOOTPRINT contributed ZERO to a memory-budget subtraction rather than refusing the budget, defended on direction -- a larger budget can only miss an exclusion, never invent one; (2) a PLACEMENT SENTENCE asserted that a route's token-time hop sits inside the memory pool, about a route whose provider chain did not resolve at all, and carried it to the product root; (3) ONE FABRIC GROUP'S idle-free reading was generalised to EVERY candidate a screen was handed, with the candidate's own group never consulted; (4) an EMPTY SEARCH -- no placement setting found -- was reported as an ESTABLISHED ABSENCE, excluding storage-backed routes exactly as hard as a reading that found the setting and read it.",

    "TWO FACTS MAKE THIS A ROW RATHER THAN FOUR NOTES, AND BOTH ARE ABOUT DETECTION. THREE OF THE FOUR WERE CAUGHT BY REVIEWERS, NOT BY ANY GATE -- the corpus is fail-closed and none of these tripped it, because each is a well-typed value in a well-typed arm. And ALL FOUR READ AS REASONABLE IN PLACE: every one had a defensible local story, three had an explicit comment defending the very substitution that was wrong, and (1) was FIXED in one direction hours before (2) shipped the same shape in another. A class whose instances are individually plausible and whose only detector is a careful reader is exactly what a ledger is for; the author cannot be the detector, because plausibility is what the author is optimising.",

    "**RECOGNITION RULE, AND IT IS AN ASYMMETRY ABOUT WHICH FORM HIDES: a widening that produces a CALMING SENTENCE is harder to see than one that produces an alarming number.** A value invites \"where did that come from\"; a sentence asserting everything is in order does not. NOBODY AUDITS REASSURANCE. Instance (1) was a number and was caught by the reviewer who found it suspicious on sight; instances (2) and (4) were prose and survived several readings including their author's, because what they emit is the shape of a conclusion rather than the shape of data. So the cheap sweep is: for every arm that RENDERS A SENTENCE or RETURNS A DEFAULT, ask what input reaches it by absence rather than by establishment -- an empty list, a false predicate, a missing lookup, a search that found nothing -- and ask whether the output would then be FALSE and REASSURING.",

    "THE REMEDY THIS INSTANCE ADDS IS A CONSTRUCTOR RULE, not a review habit: a capability probe that can refuse must return a variant whose refusal arm CARRIES NO VALUE OF THE ANSWER'S TYPE, so `device_memory = 0` has no way to be written. extdeps.nvidia.management_library models the query that way — an unsupported query yields an arm with no byte count at all — which makes the absorbed substitution unwritable rather than discouraged (DESIGN section 4b(4)). The review tell is a `try` around an observation whose `except` assigns a plausible literal to the variable the observation was for.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
